    48	## 1. Common numerical compatibility condition
    49	
    50	Keep the notation of the charged packet.  In its `F_2` total-transform
    51	marking an affine coefficient-basepoint carrier has class
    52	
    53	```text
    54	Z_J=S_0+2F-sum_(j in J)E_j,       |J|=5.              (1.1)
    55	```
    56	
    57	For two distinct classes,
    58	
    59	```text
    60	Z_J.Z_K=2-|J cap K|.                                  (1.2)
    61	```
    62	
    63	Distinct contracted curves lie over distinct target points: the fibre over
    64	one target point contains at most the one source line `{q} times P1`.
    65	Therefore their strict transforms are disjoint, and numerical coexistence
    66	requires
    67	
    68	```text
    69	|J cap K|=2.                                          (1.3)
    70	```
    71	
    72	At most one irreducible carrier can have a given class, since two distinct
    73	effective curves in that class would have intersection `Z_J^2=-3`.  Thus a
    74	family of distinct effective contracted carriers gives a family of distinct
    75	subsets satisfying (1.3).  The converse is not asserted: (1.3) is numerical
    76	compatibility, not proximity or effectivity.
