   266	## 3. What the orbit key does and does not quotient
   267	
   268	The signature (0.4) is the `W(D9)` orbit key for the **unmarked root image**.
   269	It is only a coarse bucket after adding any of the following:
   270	
   271	```text
   272	beta and actual-fibre identity;
   273	the marked original component and proximity history;
   274	attachment vertices and physical attachment points;
   275	(m,n,h,a), target-image labels, or H/R carrier labels.   (3.1)
   276	```
   277	
   278	Such decorations can destroy the odd stabilizer used in Section 1.  Exact
   279	decorated canonicalization fixes one coordinate representative of (0.4) and
